# Specs Agent Platform Work Board

This is the actionable backlog behind the [README roadmap](README.md#roadmap).
Unchecked items are planned improvements, not prerequisites for running the
current release.

Priorities:

- **P0** - security, data safety, or release blockers.
- **P1** - next-release quality and delivery work.
- **P2** - platform capabilities and maintainability.
- **P3** - longer-term product direction.

## Completed foundation

- [x] Create the uv workspace with `open-agent-core`, `open-agent-lang`, and
  `open-agent-adk` as independently packaged modules.
- [x] Keep Open Workflow and Open Agent Specification loaders separated under
  `open-agent-core` and normalize both into a framework-neutral IR.
- [x] Add Pydantic validation, `pyagentspec` validation, bindings, aliases,
  duplicate-entrypoint checks, and YAML source coordinates.
- [x] Implement the supported Open Workflow v1 execution surface: expressions,
  `set`, `call`, `switch`, `for`, `while`, `fork`, `wait`, `listen`, `raise`,
  `emit`, `if`, retry, catch, and finally.
- [x] Add deterministic local execution, HTTP calls, ChatOpenAI and Google ADK
  bridges, and optional SQLite checkpoints.
- [x] Add LangGraph and ADK compilers, MCP adapters, FastAPI runners, CLIs,
  embedded UIs, and independent Docker images.
- [x] Add OpenAI-compatible chat/models/tools APIs, health routes, CloudEvents
  intake, authentication, request limits, timeouts, and structured failures.
- [x] Add tests, conformance fixtures, Docker Compose profiles, package builds,
  Postgres-backed startup smoke tests, and environment-driven configuration.

## P0 - Security and runtime safety

- [x] **SEC-001:** Reject chunked requests that exceed `MAX_REQUEST_BYTES`
  instead of relying only on `Content-Length`.
- [x] **SEC-002:** Stop publishing Postgres on `0.0.0.0:5432` with a placeholder
  password by default until the Postgres checkpoint backend is available.
  Bound to `127.0.0.1` instead of all interfaces; the password remains a dev
  default since Postgres is unused by application code until **RUN-002**.
- [x] **SEC-003:** Add depth and document-size limits to recursive workflow task
  loading to prevent `RecursionError` and resource-exhaustion attacks.
- [x] **SEC-004:** Add configurable CORS middleware with a restrictive default.
- [x] **SEC-005:** Add configurable API rate limiting and authentication lockout.
  - Acceptance:
    - Per-client sliding-window request rate limiting returns HTTP 429 with
      `Retry-After` when the limit is exceeded.
    - Failed authentication attempts are counted per client and lock the client
      out for a configurable duration after a threshold.
    - Behavior is driven by environment variables with safe defaults and can be
      disabled explicitly.
    - Health endpoints remain reachable for orchestrators.
    - Both runners share the same ASGI middleware from `open-agent-core`.
  - Files: `open_agent_core/http_security.py`, both `runner.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium.

- [x] **SEC-006:** Add MCP subprocess sandboxing, lifecycle limits,
  cancellation, and health reporting.
  - Acceptance:
    - Command allow/deny lists and shell-interpreter blocking are configurable
      via environment variables.
    - Per-call timeouts, output-size limits, and a concurrency cap are enforced.
    - Subprocesses are terminated when the calling task is cancelled or times out.
    - A health map tracks last success/failure per binding and is exposed through
      a protected `/health/mcp` route.
    - Shared runtime logic lives in `open-agent-core`; engine packages delegate
      to it and keep only engine-specific adapters.
  - Files: `open_agent_core/mcp_runtime.py`, both `mcp.py`, both `runner.py`,
    tests, docs.
  - Complexity: large.
  - Depends on: shared module design compatible with both engines.

## P1 - Native framework compilation

Both engine compilers currently wrap a shared interpreter (`InMemoryEngine`)
instead of mapping the workflow task tree onto each framework's native
constructs: `LangGraphCompiler` builds a single linear `StateGraph` node
chain per workflow and calls back into the interpreter for every task kind,
and `AdkCompiler` only compiles `AgentIR` — there is no ADK workflow
compiler, so `AdkEngine` always delegates the whole task tree to the
interpreter. See
[docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md#current-compilation-fidelity-known-limitation)
for the detailed breakdown. The tasks below replace that shared-interpreter
wrapper with real per-engine compilers, keeping only document parsing,
validation, and a small expression/retry utility library shared between them.

Target task-kind-to-native-primitive mapping:

| Open Workflow task | LangGraph native primitive | ADK native primitive |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `do` (sequence) | linear `add_edge` chain | `SequentialAgent` |
| `switch` | `add_conditional_edges` | custom `ConditionalAgent` (`BaseAgent`) |
| `fork` | parallel fan-out/fan-in edges | `ParallelAgent` |
| `for` / `while` | loop-back conditional edge | `LoopAgent` |
| `retry` | `add_node(..., retry_policy=...)` | custom wrapper `BaseAgent` |
| `catch` / `finally` | `add_node(..., error_handler=...)` | custom wrapper `BaseAgent` |
| `call` | node invoking the compiled sub-graph/agent | sub-agent reference |
| `set` / `run` | dedicated node function | custom `BaseAgent` leaf |
| `wait` / `listen` / `raise` / `emit` | dedicated node function (no native primitive) | custom `BaseAgent` leaf (no native primitive) |

- [x] **COMPILE-001:** Extract a standalone expression evaluator and
  retry/backoff policy from `InMemoryEngine` into reusable `open-agent-core`
  modules that either native compiler can call without depending on the
  interpreter.
  - Acceptance:
    - `open_agent_core/expressions.py` exposes `evaluate(expr, context)` and
      condition helpers (`when`/`exceptWhen` semantics) used by both
      `runtime.py` and the new native compilers.
    - `open_agent_core/retry.py` exposes a framework-neutral retry/backoff
      policy (constant/linear/exponential) that both engines can translate
      into their own native retry mechanism.
    - `InMemoryEngine` is refactored to call these modules instead of owning
      the logic inline; existing behavior and tests are unchanged.
  - Files: new `open_agent_core/expressions.py`, `open_agent_core/retry.py`,
    `runtime.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium.
  - Status: completed — `expressions.py` (evaluate/resolve_value/condition_allows) and
    `retry.py` (RetryPolicy/BackoffPolicy/parse_retry_config) extracted;
    `runtime.py` delegates via backward-compatible private aliases; all tests pass.

- [x] **COMPILE-002:** LangGraph native compiler — per-task-kind node
  generation for `set`, `call`, and `run`, replacing the generic
  `execute_task` delegation for these kinds.
  - Acceptance:
    - Each `set`/`call`/`run` task compiles to its own node function that
      resolves values via `open_agent_core/expressions.py` directly, not
      through `InMemoryEngine.execute_task`.
    - Existing conformance fixtures using only these kinds produce identical
      output through the compiled graph and through `InMemoryEngine`.
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-001.
  - Status: completed — `set`/`call`/`run` compile to native node functions
    (incl. `if` gating and call dispatch parity: bound agents, handlers, HTTP);
    parity tests cover the conformance fixtures, call dispatch, and `if` gates.

- [x] **COMPILE-003:** LangGraph native `switch` mapping via
  `add_conditional_edges`.
  - Acceptance:
    - `switch` tasks compile to a routing function registered with
      `add_conditional_edges`; each branch becomes its own chain of native
      nodes rather than an interpreter call.
    - Default/fallback branches and `case`-expression branches from the Open
      Workflow v1 fixtures behave identically to the interpreter path.
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium/large.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-002.
  - Status: completed — switch routes via `add_conditional_edges` with one
    chain of native nodes per branch; case/default/when/no-match routing,
    `if` gating, and empty branches match interpreter parity (169 tests pass).

- [ ] **COMPILE-004:** LangGraph native `fork` mapping via parallel
  fan-out/fan-in edges.
  - Acceptance:
    - Fork branches compile to independent node chains from a common
      fan-out node, converging on a join node.
    - Branch output merge order is deterministic and documented; LangGraph's
      state-reducer support is used to avoid concurrent-write races.
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: large.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-002.
  - Status: completed — fork compiles to a fan-out node, per-branch chains
    writing reducer-merged `fork` channel slots, and a join that merges in
    declared branch order; `compete` resolves to the first declared branch
    (no LangGraph cancellation; documented in `docs/architecture.md`);
    interpreter `invoke`/`stream` now wrap non-dict output; if-gated and
    nested forks match interpreter parity (173 tests pass).

- [ ] **COMPILE-005:** LangGraph native `for`/`while` mapping via a
  loop-back conditional edge.
  - Acceptance:
    - The loop body compiles to a node chain with a continuation router that
      loops back via `add_conditional_edges` or exits forward.
    - Loop-variable scoping matches current interpreter semantics
      (**SPEC-002**); a configurable max-iteration guard prevents runaway
      loops from a malformed condition.
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: large.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-002.
  - Status: completed — `for` tasks compile to a setup node, body chain, and
    continuation router looping back via `add_conditional_edges` (loop state
    in a reducer-merged `loop` channel); task-level `while` breaks per
    iteration; loop variables are restored at exit (SPEC-002 scoping);
    `MAX_LOOP_ITERATIONS` (default 10000, compiler-overridable) guards
    runaway loops; empty bodies/iterables and nested loops match interpreter
    parity. Task-level `while` on kind-`do` tasks stays delegated (the
    interpreter does not loop them). 180 tests pass.

- [ ] **COMPILE-006:** LangGraph native `retry`/`catch`/`finally` mapping
  via `add_node(..., retry_policy=..., error_handler=...)`.
  - Acceptance:
    - `retry` config (`max_attempts`, backoff strategy) maps onto
      LangGraph's `RetryPolicy` using the shared `open_agent_core/retry.py`
      policy from **COMPILE-001**.
    - `catch` branches are wired as the node's `error_handler`; `finally`
      tasks execute on both the success and error paths via explicit edges.
    - Error aliasing/filtering semantics from the interpreter path are
      preserved.
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: large.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-001, COMPILE-002.
  - Status: completed — static retry configs map to LangGraph `RetryPolicy`
    (constant/linear/exponential, jitter off, retry-on-any-exception); catch
    wires as the node's `error_handler` with the interpreter's
    errors.with/when/exceptWhen filtering and `as` aliasing; finally chains
    run on success, handled, and unhandled paths, with the unhandled path
    re-raising a fresh exception (LangGraph swallows re-raised originals it
    already routed); dynamic retry conditions stay delegated; docs updated
    (184 tests pass).

- [ ] **COMPILE-007:** LangGraph native leaf tasks without a framework
  primitive (`wait`, `listen`, `raise`, `emit`) as dedicated node functions.
  - Acceptance:
    - Each kind compiles to its own small node function using the shared
      expression evaluator; behavior matches the interpreter path.
    - `docs/architecture.md` documents why these remain node-function-based
      rather than mapped to a native LangGraph primitive.
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, tests, `docs/architecture.md`.
  - Complexity: medium.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-001, COMPILE-002.

- [ ] **COMPILE-008:** Retire `InMemoryEngine` as the LangGraph engine's
  production execution path.
  - Acceptance:
    - `LangGraphEngine`/`LangGraphCompiler` no longer call
      `InMemoryEngine.execute_task`/`invoke` for any task kind covered by
      **COMPILE-002** through **COMPILE-007**.
    - `InMemoryEngine` remains available for the core CLI's offline
      validate/dry-run path and as the parity-test reference implementation
      (**COMPILE-014**).
  - Files: `open_agent_lang/compiler.py`, `open_agent_lang/runner.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-002 through COMPILE-007.

- [ ] **COMPILE-009:** ADK native workflow compiler skeleton —
  `WorkflowIR` to a `BaseAgent` composite tree.
  - Acceptance:
    - New `open_agent_adk/workflow_compiler.py` maps `do` (sequence) to
      `SequentialAgent`, `fork` to `ParallelAgent`, `for`/`while` to
      `LoopAgent`, and `call` to the already-compiled `LlmAgent` for the
      referenced agent (or a nested compiled sub-workflow).
    - `set`/`run` compile to minimal custom `BaseAgent` leaves that mutate
      session state via the shared expression evaluator.
  - Files: new `open_agent_adk/workflow_compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: large.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-001.

- [ ] **COMPILE-010:** ADK native `switch` mapping via a custom
  `ConditionalAgent`.
  - Acceptance:
    - A `BaseAgent` subclass evaluates branch conditions with the shared
      expression evaluator and dispatches to exactly one matching
      sub-agent, since ADK has no built-in conditional composite.
    - Behavior matches the interpreter path for the Open Workflow v1
      `switch` fixtures.
  - Files: `open_agent_adk/workflow_compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-009.

- [ ] **COMPILE-011:** ADK native `retry`/`catch`/`finally` mapping via a
  custom wrapper `BaseAgent`.
  - Acceptance:
    - A wrapper agent applies the shared `open_agent_core/retry.py` policy
      around its wrapped sub-agent, since ADK has no built-in retry
      composite.
    - Catch/finally semantics match the LangGraph mapping (**COMPILE-006**)
      and the interpreter path.
  - Files: `open_agent_adk/workflow_compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: large.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-001, COMPILE-009.

- [ ] **COMPILE-012:** ADK native leaf tasks without a composite primitive
  (`wait`, `listen`, `raise`, `emit`) as small `BaseAgent` leaves.
  - Acceptance:
    - Each kind compiles to its own minimal `BaseAgent`, mirroring
      **COMPILE-007**'s LangGraph leaves for behavioral parity.
  - Files: `open_agent_adk/workflow_compiler.py`, tests.
  - Complexity: medium.
  - Depends on: COMPILE-001, COMPILE-009.

- [ ] **COMPILE-013:** Retire `InMemoryEngine` as the ADK engine's
  production execution path.
  - Acceptance:
    - `AdkEngine.invoke`/`stream`/`execute_task` run the compiled
